{
  "dom_id": "question-127236",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Find the function $L(x),$ the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=4.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $L(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(4)+{f}^{′}(4)(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have $f(4)=-5$ and ${f}^{′}(4)=-7,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =-5-7(x-4) \\\\  & =-5-7x+28 \\\\  & =-7x+23.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
